From 4b8c5919ce1f21d7b6be5b67f051e052502bd7df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:35:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/32] feat(qwen4_exp): native NVFP4 PLE table (host-resident,
 dequant in gather)

text_config.ple_embedding_dtype="nvfp4" (as the local-inference-lab QAD
checkpoint ships it) now keeps the n-gram table NVFP4 in pinned host memory:
one 90-byte row per id (80 bytes of e2m1 pairs, low nibble first, then 10
fp8 block scales), and the gather kernel dequantizes e2m1 * block_scale *
weight_scale_2 in fp32 before the bf16 store. Table 26.8 GiB instead of
47.7 GiB for the FP8 re-code, and no re-code error (1.38% rel-RMS removed).

Loader: shard_N.weight -> row bytes [0, D/2), shard_N.weight_scale -> row
bytes [D/2, D/2+D/16), ngram_embedding.weight_scale_2 -> fp32 buffer; raises
on an NVFP4 tensor when the table was not built NVFP4, and on a code/scale
shard count mismatch. Offload-only (raises without --ple-offload-embedding).

GPU check (RTX PRO 4000, sm_120): 200k real rows bit-identical to
dequantize_nvfp4 rounded to bf16; out-of-range ids write zeros.
Dry-run harness now mirrors the offload flags and checks PLE row coverage.
